      "required_resolution": "Close the worker ownership handoff before allowing training, retaining fresh PID/start/command/group identity across launcher death. Unknown worker ownership must remain unknown rather than become absence. Preserve safe exact-target signaling and no-retry behavior.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "source_reason": "worker_anchors is populated only from descendants(current, proc.pid). A reparented worker is absent from that set. With a published launch record, signal_group sees live group members but no matching anchor and raises before sending TERM or KILL; the exception fallback proves only the outer Popen group. Without the launch record, worker_pid stays None and worker_group_absent is reported true without establishing whether a worker was spawned.",
      "title": "Worker ownership is lost if the launcher exits before the first worker snapshot",
      "trigger": "The launcher successfully starts the separate worker session, then exits ungracefully before the observer captures a ps snapshot containing that worker as its descendant. This can occur before or after worker-launch.json publication.",
      "verification": "Source control-flow review only; no process launch or failure injection performed."
    },
